# Web Traffic Analytics

## Project Overview

This project analyzes website traffic data to understand user behavior and engagement patterns. It identifies important metrics such as page views, session duration, traffic sources, and drop-off points to help improve website performance.

---

## Objectives

- Analyze website visitor behavior.
- Measure user engagement.
- Identify drop-off points.
- Evaluate traffic sources.
- Generate actionable recommendations.

---

## Dataset Features

| Column | Description |
|----------|------------|
| UserID | Unique visitor ID |
| Page | Visited page |
| SessionDuration | Time spent on site (seconds) |
| PageViews | Number of pages viewed |
| TrafficSource | Source of visitor traffic |
| ExitPage | Whether user exited the site |

---

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas

---

## Project Structure

```text
web-traffic-analytics/
│
├── web_traffic_analysis.py
├── website_traffic.csv
├── traffic_report.csv
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
```

---

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/web-traffic-analytics.git
cd web-traffic-analytics
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## Run Project

```bash
python web_traffic_analysis.py
```

---

## Key Metrics Analyzed

- Total Users
- Total Page Views
- Average Session Duration
- Most Visited Pages
- Traffic Sources
- User Drop-Off Points

---

## Sample Insights

- Identify high-performing pages.
- Understand visitor engagement.
- Detect pages with high exit rates.
- Analyze traffic acquisition channels.

---

## Recommendations

- Improve pages with high drop-off rates.
- Optimize content on low-engagement pages.
- Strengthen successful traffic channels.
- Enhance user navigation and experience.

---

## Output

Generated report:

```text
traffic_report.csv
```

containing summarized website traffic insights.

